 I'd be happy to help you create a function that accepts text and posts it to a Slack channel using the Slack API in JavaScript. Here's an example of how you might implement this:

```javascript
const axios = require('axios'); // Make sure to install 'axios' package using npm or yarn

async function postMessageToSlack(text, channel) {
  try {
    const options = {
      method: 'post',
      url: `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage`,
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      data: {
        text,
        channel,
        token: process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN, // Replace with your bot token
      },
    };

    const response = await axios(options);
    if (response.data.ok) {
      console.log(`Message posted to #${channel}: ${text}`);
    } else {
      throw new Error(`Error posting message to Slack: ${response.data.error}`);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error posting message to Slack: ${error.message}`);
  }
}

// Usage example:
postMessageToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

This function uses the `axios` library for making HTTP requests. It accepts two arguments - the text you want to post and the channel name where you want to post it. The helper function sets up the required options for the Slack API request and sends the POST request. In case of a successful response, it logs a message indicating that the message has been posted to the specified channel. If there is an error, it logs the error message.

You can adjust the verbosity by modifying the logging statements according to your needs. Also, make sure to replace `process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` with your actual bot token.

