    %Process lines
    words1_line = lower(strsplit(line1));
    words2_line = lower(strsplit(line2));
    uniqueWords_line = setdiff(words1_line, words2_line);

    %Combine unique words with previous ones
    uniqueWords = [uniqueWords; uniqueWords_line];
end

%Close files
fclose(fid1);
fclose(fid2);

%Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);
```

This implementation reads each line of the text files separately, processes them, and merges the unique words together. This approach helps reduce the memory consumption and allows handling larger text files.

