 To write a C++ program for bubble sort using minimal memory and with error avoidance, follow these steps:

1. Define the function `bubbleSort` that takes an integer array as an argument and sorts it using the bubble sort algorithm. This function will not use dynamic memory allocation to minimize memory usage.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                // Swap elements
                int temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                arr[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

