 I'm glad you found my assistance helpful so far! Regarding your request, here are some alternative words for "unpunctual":
- Late
- Tardy
- Delayed
- Behind schedule
- Running late
As for adverbs indicating different levels of lateness based on your table, here they are:
- Slightly late: Somewhat unfashionably late, Barely on time, A bit behind schedule
- Moderately late: Fairly late, Quite tardy, Reasonably behind schedule
- Very late: Extremely tardy, Highly delayed, Exceedingly behind schedule
Now, let me provide you with a Java program code snippet that calculates the duration between two dates in different time zones, taking into account the time difference between them:
```java
import java.time.*;
import java.time.zone.ZoneId;
public class DateDurationCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Define the dates and time zones
        ZonedDateTime date1 = ZonedDateTime.of(2022, Month.JANUARY, 1, 10, 0, 0, 0, ZoneId.of("Europe/Paris"));
        ZonedDateTime date2 = ZonedDateTime.of(2022, Month.JANUARY, 1, 15, 30, 0, 0, ZoneId.of("America/Los_Angeles"));
        // Calculate the duration between the two dates
        ZonedDateTime start = date1.withZoneSameInstant(ZoneId.systemDefault());
        ZonedDateTime end = date2.withZoneSameInstant(ZoneId.systemDefault());
        Duration duration = Duration.between(start, end);
        // Print the result
        System.out.printf("The duration between %s and %s is: %d hours, %d minutes%n", date1, date2, duration.getHours(), duration.getMinutes());
    }
}
```
